  "schema:keywords": [
    "influenza",
    "Primary Endpoint(s) 1. Identification of fine-grained innate and possible adaptive immune signatures (traditional immune parameters measurements + array-based gene expression) at all time points after primary vaccination at Day 0, within the first 24 hrs after boosting at day 21, and at D28, D42, and D100. 2. Measurement of adaptive immune responses [microneutralization (MN) titers] at Day 0, D7, D21, 28, and D100 post first vaccination (D0) and post second vaccination (D21) with or without adjuvant. 3. Correlation of pre-vaccination (D0) and post-vaccination (2-24 hrs, D7, D21 [0-24h], D28, D42, and D100 immune signatures to adaptive immune responses [microneutralization (MN) titers] on D0, D7, D21, D28, and D100 after vaccination with or without adjuvant. 3. Correlation of pre-vaccination (D0) and post-vaccination (2-24 hrs, D7, D21 [0-24h], D28, D42, and D100 immune signatures to clinical observations especially safety related local and systemic events recorded on the targeted CRF. 4. Comparison of kinetics and magnitude of vaccine-specific plasmablasts (D7, D21 and D28, D42) and memory B cells (D0, D21, D42 and D100) in participants receiving the vaccines with or without adjuvant. 5. Identification of correlative and predictive signatures of immune responses using data obtained at D0 before vaccination, and at 2-24 hrs as well as D7 and D21 days (0-24 hrs) after vaccination that correlate with MN titers at D100 in participants receiving the vaccines with or without adjuvant. Exploratory Endpoint(s) 1. T cell follicular response dynamics using flow cytometric analysis at D7, D21, D28, and D42 in participants receiving the vaccines with or without adjuvant. 2. Identification of signatures of immune responses at D0, first 24 hrs, D7, and D21 (2-24 hrs) after each vaccination that correlate with antigen-specific T cell responses at D1, D7, D21, D22, D28, and D42; and T cell follicular responses at D1, D7, D21, D22, D28, and D42 in participants receiving the vaccines with or without adjuvant. 3. Correlation of MN titers 21 days after each vaccination with antigen-specific T cell responses at D1, D7, D21, D22, D28, and D42 and T cell follicular responses at D1, D7, D21, D22, D28, and D42 in participants receiving the vaccines with or without adjuvant.",
    "NIH Center for Human Immunology, Autoimmunity and Inflammation (CHI)",
